2026-09-07T01:59:27.664Z [dev/opencode] (stderr) # Experiments
2026-09-07T01:59:27.664Z [dev/opencode] (stderr) Each folder here is a **Ralph target repository**: at minimum a requirements file (see root `README.md` → *Required Requirements File*) and `ralph/epic.md`. Ralph bootstraps the rest of `ralph/*` (prompts, `task-status.json`, etc.) when you first point Kanban at that directory.
2026-09-07T01:59:27.664Z [dev/opencode] (stderr) You may add a **`material/`** subdirectory for screenshots and other static reference files (not app source). That keeps curated example assets separate from generated code under `src/`, `dist/`, and similar. Example: [`experiments/todo/material/`](todo/material/).
