2026-09-07T02:32:26.069Z [plan/opencode] ## Next task — full implementation-ready description
2026-09-07T02:32:26.069Z [plan/opencode] ### Task 39 — Port directed-send main switch to production
2026-09-07T02:32:26.069Z [plan/opencode] **What and why.** The current production app has no session-graph or directed-send layer: program payloads are broadcast to every window over the global `BroadcastChannel` named `presentation` (`src/Present/Broadcast.ts`, `app/utils/Broadcast.ts`), `electron/main.cjs` opens only a single window with no session/child ownership, and `DeckBuilder` has no Presentation control bar. The epic's next-cycle items C (close removes child), A (End blanks Present), and D (on-program thumbnail) all assume a main-process session graph that pushes payloads to *selected* Present children only — the baseline confirmed on v0.1.7-pr.15. The authoritative reference implementation is the POC at `~/Downloads/poster-directed-send-poc` (`src/mainSwitch.js` + `src/mainSwitch.test.js`): a pure, DOM-free session module that must now exist in production. Both the epic's suite map and its risk note ("harness must target real main session module, not only POC") point here, so this task is the foundation for Items C, A, and D.
2026-09-07T02:32:26.069Z [plan/opencode] **Implementation guidance.**
2026-09-07T02:32:26.069Z [plan/opencode] 1. Add a production session module — recommended at `server/main-switch.cjs` written in CommonJS so `electron/main.cjs` and `server/index.js` can `require()` it as-is. It must import nothing from Electron, the DOM, or BroadcastChannel so Jest can exercise it with an injected transport; keep it dependency-free and framework-agnostic (mirror the POC `createMainSwitch` export shape).
2026-09-07T02:32:26.070Z [plan/opencode] 2. Model the module on POC `mainSwitch.js`: a `sessions` map; minted `sessionId`/`presentId` (never reused after close); per-session present registry with `label`, window handle, and `lastPayload`; and the four fixed channel functions `deckCommand` (register / spawn / send / close / list), `presentPush` (push to one present), `presentEvent` (ready replays last payload; closed unregisters), and `deckEvent` (deploy `restore` and `child-closed` to the owning deck).
2026-09-07T02:32:26.070Z [plan/opencode] 3. Define an injectable `presentTransport` interface (`open`, `push`, `close`, optional `isClosed`) that maps to the Electron `BrowserWindow`/`webContents` abstraction; the real Electron wiring is deliberately deferred to task 40, so this module must be fully testable via a mock transport.
2026-09-07T02:32:26.070Z [plan/opencode] 4. Preserve POC semantics exactly: send resolves `presentIds` only within the named session (missing/unknown ids are no-ops); `all: true` targets that session's children only; `close` unregisters and emits exactly one `child-closed` deck-event with an updated child snapshot; closing one of N leaves the others registered and sendable; `ready` replays the present's last payload.
2026-09-07T02:32:26.070Z [plan/opencode] 5. Stand up the new Jest harness for the epic's proposed `tests/` tree: a minimal standalone `jest.config.cjs` runnable via `npx jest --config jest.config.cjs` using the `node` test environment and `roots: ['<rootDir>/tests']`, plus the `mockWebContentsSend()` fixture that records `{ presentId, channel, payload }` and never touches a real BrowserWindow. (Do not rely on `react-scripts` which roots under `src/`.)
2026-09-07T02:32:26.070Z [plan/opencode] 6. Port the POC test scenarios to `tests/unit/main/session-graph.test.ts` with describes for register/spawn/send/list/close covering the six POC routing guarantees (directed targeting, all-my-children only, cross-session no-op, close drops from list, replay-on-ready). Keep the ported module and tests separate from any POC copy; the POC stays a reference, not the shipped code.
2026-09-07T02:32:26.070Z [plan/opencode] **Testing steps.** Run `npx jest --config jest.config.cjs tests/unit/main`. Assertions that fail on today's architecture (global broadcast, no session graph): after `spawn` + `send({presentIds:[id]})`, the mock transport recorded the payload only for that present id; after `close` + `list`, the closed id is gone and a single `child-closed` deck-event fired; `send` targeting a closed id or `send({all:true})` after close records zero pushes to the closed child; closing one of N leaves the other child pushable.
2026-09-07T02:32:26.070Z [plan/opencode] **Acceptance criteria.**
2026-09-07T02:32:26.070Z [plan/opencode] - `server/main-switch.cjs` (or agreed equivalent) exists, requires no Electron/DOM/BroadcastChannel at import, and exposes the four channel functions plus createSession/spawn/send/close/list/getSessions.
2026-09-07T02:32:26.070Z [plan/opencode] - Session-graph semantics match the POC reference and are enforced by `tests/unit/main/session-graph.test.ts`, green under the new standalone Jest config.
2026-09-07T02:32:26.070Z [plan/opencode] - `mockWebContentsSend()` fixture exists and is reused by later A/C tests.
2026-09-07T02:32:26.070Z [plan/opencode] - No `BroadcastChannel('presentation')` slide-payload usage is introduced in this module.
2026-09-07T02:32:26.070Z [plan/opencode] - Code follows existing repo conventions (CommonJS for the server/electron layer; no new dependencies required).
