2026-09-07T05:33:14.379Z [dev/opencode] - `SessionTransport.ts` (browser fallback path) registers via HTTP relay (`/api/poster/deck-command`), but Electron uses the IPC path listed above.
2026-09-07T05:33:14.379Z [dev/opencode] - Playwright Electron API: `app.waitForEvent('window')` and `app.firstWindow()` are the correct window-creation primitives; `app.windows()` also exists. `deck-session-ready` is a hidden `<span>` (not visible), so must assert `data-ready="true"` via `toHaveAttribute`, not visibility.
2026-09-07T05:33:14.379Z [dev/opencode] - Tests destroy sandboxes in `finally`; app close via `closeApp()` is safe when already exited.
2026-09-07T05:33:14.379Z [dev/opencode] - Existing `playwright.electron.config.ts` uses `testMatch: /electron-.*\.spec\.ts/` and `workers: 1`, so all new specs are auto-discovered and run serially.
