2026-09-07T05:38:27.815Z [plan/opencode] ## Task 10 — Fix Electron Home "Change..." library re-point (implementation-ready)
2026-09-07T05:38:27.815Z [plan/opencode] **Repo:** `/Users/hpractv/ralph-runs/poster` only. Never implement in `izep/ralph-gui`.
2026-09-07T05:38:27.815Z [plan/opencode] **What and why.** The Home library "Change..." control must re-point the library root as the only in-app way operators change `~/.poster` to another folder (requirements.md §3 "Home library UX" and §5 "Library durability"). Today the control is broken in every packaged/Electron build: `src/HomePage.tsx:58` calls `window.prompt('Library folder', ...)`, and Electron renderers throw `Error: prompt() is not supported.` (recorded in `ralph/qa-report.md`, finding 2, during task 9). The button errors before showing anything, so packaged operators cannot re-point the library. Browser/Remix usage is fine because `window.prompt` works there.
2026-09-07T05:38:27.815Z [plan/opencode] **Implementation guidance.**
2026-09-07T05:38:27.815Z [plan/opencode] 1. `electron/main.cjs` (via `dialog` from electron): register one IPC handler, e.g. `poster:choose-library-dir`, invoked from the Home window. Use `dialog.showOpenDialog({ properties: ['openDirectory', 'createDirectory'], defaultPath })` where `defaultPath` is the active library root (fall back to `app.getPath('home')`). Return the selected absolute path, or `null`/`undefined` when the user cancels. Do not return a `filePaths[0]` unless one was picked.
2026-09-07T05:38:27.815Z [plan/opencode] 2. `electron/preload.cjs`: expose `chooseLibraryDir: () => ipcRenderer.invoke('poster:choose-library-dir')` on the existing `window.poster` bridge. Keep `contextIsolation: true`, `nodeIntegration: false`, and `sandbox: true` unchanged — do not widen the security surface. Do not pass any raw input to the dialog.
2026-09-07T05:38:27.815Z [plan/opencode] 3. `src/HomePage.tsx` `changeLibraryRoot`:
2026-09-07T05:38:27.815Z [plan/opencode]    - If `window.poster` (the preload bridge) is present, call `await window.poster.chooseLibraryDir()`; if it returns nothing/null, exit without any POST (cancel = no-op).
2026-09-07T05:38:27.815Z [plan/opencode]    - Otherwise keep the current `window.prompt` behavior as the plain-browser fallback.
2026-09-07T05:38:27.815Z [plan/opencode]    - Preserve the existing contract: no POST when the chosen root equals the current root; POST JSON `{ libraryRoot: path }` to the `remixDataUrl('/library/settings', REMIX_ROUTE_ID.librarySettings)` endpoint; on `!ok` or missing `libraryRoot`, surface the route error via the existing `window.alert`; on success update `libraryRoot` state and bump `libraryRefreshKey`.
2026-09-07T05:38:27.815Z [plan/opencode] 4. Verify the chosen path passes the existing server-side validation (must be an absolute directory; `app/utils/library-root.server.ts` rejects relative/file paths) — no server-side change is expected.
2026-09-07T05:38:27.815Z [plan/opencode] 5. Run the theme bridge pattern already used in `src/utils/useTheme` for the same `window.poster` detection so renderer code stays consistent.
2026-09-07T05:38:27.815Z [plan/opencode] **Testing steps.**
2026-09-07T05:38:27.815Z [plan/opencode] - `cd /Users/hpractv/ralph-runs/poster`
2026-09-07T05:38:27.815Z [plan/opencode] - `pnpm run build:remix` (needed for production-server Electron smoke — a stale dev-runtime `build/` causes the documented SSR 500).
2026-09-07T05:38:27.815Z [plan/opencode] - Manual: `pnpm run electron` → Home → click `Change...` → OS folder picker opens → pick a new folder → Home shows the new `Library folder:` path; picker cancel leaves the current root; old folder is untouched.
2026-09-07T05:38:27.815Z [plan/opencode] - `CI=true pnpm exec react-scripts test --watchAll=false --runInBand` (existing 38 suites / 226 tests stay green).
2026-09-07T05:38:27.815Z [plan/opencode] - `CI=true pnpm run test:e2e:remix` (browser fallback stays green).
2026-09-07T05:38:27.815Z [plan/opencode] - `pnpm exec playwright test --config=playwright.electron.config.ts` (the new bridge must not break the existing 8 Electron specs).
2026-09-07T05:38:27.815Z [plan/opencode] **Acceptance criteria.**
2026-09-07T05:38:27.816Z [plan/opencode] - Clicking `Change...` in the packaged Electron app opens a native directory picker (no `prompt() is not supported` error).
2026-09-07T05:38:27.816Z [plan/opencode] - Selecting a folder re-points the active library root via the same `/library/settings` POST and the old folder is left untouched.
2026-09-07T05:38:27.816Z [plan/opencode] - Cancelling the picker is a no-op; choosing the current root does not POST.
2026-09-07T05:38:27.816Z [plan/opencode] - Plain browsers (Remix dev) still use the `window.prompt` fallback and re-point identically.
2026-09-07T05:38:27.816Z [plan/opencode] - `contextIsolation`/`nodeIntegration`/sandbox settings unchanged; `tsc --noEmit` and the full Jest + Remix + Electron suites pass.
